# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile's builder stage copies the
# entire local working tree — including a Windows-installed node_modules (if
# one exists locally) — into the Linux build context. Since that COPY runs
# AFTER `npm install` in the Dockerfile, it can overwrite the correctly
# Linux-built node_modules (and Prisma's platform-specific query-engine
# binary) with Windows-native binaries. The app still boots fine (nothing
# touches Prisma until the first real request), but the first actual
# database query then crashes the process immediately and hard enough that
# no log line makes it out — which matches this service's exact symptom:
# clean "Ready"/"live" logs, then a silent, request-triggered 502 with zero
# backend log output. This is the single most likely root cause found so
# far; everything else checked (port, region, service identity, Render
# platform status) came back clean.
node_modules
.next
.git
.env
.env.local
.env.production
npm-debug.log*
